<< /A 39 0 R /Alt (Nomogram graphic showing how points are assigned for T2DM duration, preoperative day-1 fasting plasma glucose, postoperative fasting time, ASA grade above two, and previous prolonged insulin treatment to estimate total risk.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 32 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 40 0 R /Alt (ROC curve comparing training cohort \(red line\) and internal test cohort \(blue line\), showing sensitivity versus false positive rate. Area under the curve is 0.817 for training and 0.751 for test.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 41 0 R /Alt (Pair of calibration plots labeled A and B compare observed probability versus predicted probability from zero to one, featuring dashed blue lines for ideal predictions, red lines for apparent predictions, and green lines for bias-corrected predictions. Legend and axes are clearly labeled.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 33 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 42 0 R /Alt (Panel A and panel B each show a line chart comparing net benefit versus high risk threshold and cost:benefit ratio for three approaches: Mode, All, and None. The Mode line is shown in red and stays above zero across most thresholds, while All and None lines, in gray and black, decline more sharply. Panel A reaches a higher net benefit peak than panel B, as shown by the y-axis range. Legends identifying the lines are in both panels.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
